g flag, and opening the map consumes the flag and shows the menu. Natural save: 0x0a.","confidence":"likely","evidence":"story command sets it with pending bit; menu builder reads ROM row [mode][number] and filters by obtained entries; new-game block 0 vs story block 0x0a"},{"name":"area number","medium":"cart SRAM","offset":20532,"size":2,"encoding":"u16le","type":"unsigned","meaning":"Current area/scene number used by the story script to branch; areas 0x30/0x36/0x39/0x3c/0x3d/0x4c place the party at map point 0. Cleared-game save resets it to 0x30. Natural save: 0x30.","confidence":"likely","evidence":"story command sets it; several scene routines compare it; map-clear routine creates point 0 for those areas; new-game default 0x30"},{"name":"map location","medium":"cart SRAM","offset":20534,"size":2,"encoding":"u16le","type":"unsigned","meaning":"Index (0-39) of the map point where the party stands on the chapter map; loading puts it into both the cursor and the current-location variables. Natural save: 0x11 (point 17).","confidence":"confirmed","evidence":"moving right on the map changed the live value 0x11->0x1b; d-pad code moves among active points and wraps 0..39; loader restores cursor and location; party shown on point 17 in the screenshot","constraint":{"kind":"unsigned-range","maximum":39,"minimum":0}},{"name":"console-memory byte","medium":"cart SRAM","offset":20536,"size":2,"encoding":"u16le (u8 used)","type":"bytes","meaning":"First byte of 10 bytes the game reads from the console's built-in memory at new game (the same read can also unlock an extra move bit for the first character). Saved and loaded but NOT covered by the check value, and nothing ever reads it back, so it has no effect. Natural save: 0.","confidence":"guessed","evidence":"new-game code reads the block and stores byte 0; writer copies it without adding to the check; no reader found in the analyzed code; excluded from the recomputed check"},{"name":"check value","medium":"cart SRAM","off